+`.env` uses the usual dotenv syntax: `KEY=value`, optional single or double quotes around the value, an optional leading `export `, and `#` comment lines. Unquoted values may end with an inline ` # comment`.
+
+## Diagnosing configuration
+
+Run `python -m payhook doctor` to print every setting with its effective value and where it came from (`environment`, `.env` or `default`). Secret values (`PAYHOOK_API_TOKEN`, `PAYHOOK_WEBHOOK_SECRET`) are redacted: only the type prefix and length are shown. The output is safe to paste into a support ticket.
+
+`python -m payhook check` reports only which required settings are missing and exits non-zero if any are.
 
